<title>UK: Royal Sun says shareholders approve buyback.</title>
<headline>Royal Sun says shareholders approve buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal &amp; Sun Alliance Insurance Group Plc said on Friday that shareholders at its annual meeting had approved a resolution giving the company authority to buy back up to five percent of its issued ordinary share capital.</p>
<p>The buyback cannot be undertaken until after Royal &amp; Sun's first quarter results on May 20.</p>
<p>The company said at the time of its annual results in March that it had decided to seek permission for the buyback in anticipation of continued strengthening of its capital position.</p>
<p>Deputy chairman Roger Taylor also hinted it could be repeated in the future.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
